  "comment": [
    "Single source of the skipped-test allowlists used by the Unity test gates.",
    "Read with Get-NUnitAllowedSkippedTests in scripts/read-nunit-test-result.ps1.",
    "These tests are intentionally environment-dependent diagnostics: a clean runner may lack local corpus data,",
    "graphics, optional parity tooling, or non-Linux native probes. Do not add core importer, playback, physics,",
    "or inconclusive tests here; new names must fail the gate until reviewed.",
    "match: exact = the full test name; prefix = the name itself or its parameterized cases (name + '(');",
    "explicit = an [Explicit] test admitted when the gate's explicitPolicy is 'listed'.",
    "explicitPolicy: listed = [Explicit] skips must be listed with match 'explicit'; any = every [Explicit] skip is admitted;",
    "none = [Explicit] skips get no special admission."
  ],
